  "id": "COMPOUND:43202 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One may interact with CCRF-HSB-2. The compound is linked to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is a target of multiple molecules, including Oleamide and Erysimoside. These targets are themselves linked to CCRF-HSB-2, indicating a possible pathway through the SDR family. The final scores for all three paths are similar, suggesting a consistent level of confidence in the relationship. The mechanism appears to involve the SDR family as a mediator, with the compound acting as a substrate or activator of these enzymes, which in turn modulate the activity of CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence supports a direct interaction through the SDR family, but the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple targets within the SDR family suggests that the compound may influence multiple pathways, potentially leading to complex effects on CCRF-HSB-2.",
